+// Expression-template vector library (C++20, header-only).
+//
+// Operand ownership: every expression node is a small value that holds its
+// operands as follows.
+//   - lvalue Vec        -> non-owning reference (VecRef). The Vec must outlive
+//                          the expression, and later writes to it show through.
+//   - rvalue Vec        -> takes over the buffer (VecOwned); nothing is copied.
+//   - any expression    -> stored by value, lvalue or rvalue, so an expression
+//                          built from a local expression can be returned.
+// VecOwned shares its buffer by reference count, so copying an expression never
+// allocates, whatever it contains. To return an expression over a named local
+// Vec, std::move that Vec into it; a named Vec is an lvalue and is referenced.
+//
+// Sizes are checked when a node is built and again by size(), which walks the
+// tree: an operand Vec may have been reassigned to another size in between.
+// Evaluation checks once, then reads elements through the unchecked get().
